{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And your offspring whom etc.</b> The meaning is that Joseph is not counted in the place of three tribes but in the place of two. Accordingly, the tribe of Joseph is no longer counted in the tally of the tribes apart from the tribe of Ephraim and the tribe of Manasseh, and so indeed we find." "<b>And there is</b> for us to investigate this: why did Jacob remove Joseph from the tally of the tribes? For we find that he was not counted among the tribes — only Ephraim and Manasseh. And why should he not also be counted, so that there would be fourteen tribes together with Levi? For HaShem said to him (Genesis 35:11) that two additional tribes would come from him — not that the name of Joseph would be uprooted. Also, one needs to know: who told Jacob that the two nations that HaShem said would come from him are the sons of Joseph and not the sons of his other sons? It would have been more fitting for him to suppose and say that they are Peretz and Zerach, who are exceedingly distinguished, for in truth they are the chain of royalty." "Perhaps because the sons of Judah were alluded to in what was further said to him there: ״וּמְלָכִים מֵחֲלָצֶיךָ יֵצֵאוּ״ (Genesis 35:11). But who is to say that HaShem's intent in saying ״וּמְלָכִים מֵחֲלָצֶיךָ״ etc. is this and something else as well — perhaps the very same ״גּוֹי וּקְהַל גּוֹיִם״ are themselves the kings. And further, who is to say that these words were not spoken about the sons of the other brothers?" "<b>However,</b> when we gain insight into the matter as stated by the Creator, who said to him in prophecy: ״גּוֹי וּקְהַל גּוֹיִם יִהְיֶה מִמֶּךָּ וּמְלָכִים מֵחֲלָצֶיךָ יֵצֵאוּ״ (Genesis 35:11), the plain sense of the verse indicates that it is about Jacob Himself that He speaks — that from him they will go forth, not from his sons." "<b>Rather,</b> one must know the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Zohar vol. 1, 170b) that Joseph is the aspect of the soul of Jacob. This is what Scripture alludes to in saying (Genesis 37:2) ״אֵלֶּה תּוֹלְדוֹת יַעֲקֹב יוֹסֵף״, and as it says (Psalms 77:16) ״בְּנֵי יַעֲקֹב וְיוֹסֵף״. And the masters of truth alluded that he is the aspect of the filling of the vav, and the filling is as the letter itself. On the basis of this introduction all the fine points will be resolved, for Joseph is the aspect of Jacob and is called by the rank of father to the tribes, as is likewise indicated in the verse ״בְּנֵי יַעֲקֹב וְיוֹסֵף״. Accordingly, when HaShem said to Jacob that additional sons would come forth from him — this Jacob, this is Joseph. For this reason He did not clothe the prophecy upon his other sons, and for this reason He was precise to say ״שְׁנֵי בָנֶיךָ etc. לִי הֵם״ — meaning, at the rank of sons of Jacob, not at the rank of sons of his sons. And for this reason He added an explanation and said ״כִּרְאוּבֵן וְשִׁמְעוֹן״, and from now on Joseph is at the rank of father like Jacob, and the father is not counted together with the children under one category, just as Jacob is not counted together with the tribes."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {3 "The reading of this comment hinges on the supposition that the plain sense points to Jacob himself; the text appears slightly elliptical and is rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:04.256152104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}